    "data": {
      "title": "Binary Logic: Bitwise Gate Cascade",
      "topics": [],
      "solution": "n=int(input())\nx=int(input())&255\nfor _ in range(n):\n    g,o=input().split()\n    o=int(o)&255\n    if g=='BUFFER': pass\n    elif g=='NOT': x=255-x\n    elif g=='AND': x&=o\n    elif g=='OR': x|=o\n    elif g=='NAND': x=255-(x&o)\n    elif g=='NOR': x=255-(x|o)\n    elif g=='XOR': x^=o\n    elif g=='XNOR': x=255-(x^o)\nprint(x)",
      "statement": "An 8-bit value is transformed by a cascade of logic gates.\nEach gate is applied to every bit of the current value, using an 8-bit operand.\nBUFFER leaves the value unchanged; NOT inverts all 8 bits.\nAND, OR, NAND, NOR, XOR and XNOR combine the current value with the operand bit by bit.\nStart from the given initial value, apply the gates in order, and print the final 8-bit value as a decimal integer.",
