    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">An 8-bit value is transformed by a cascade of logic gates.<br>Each gate is applied to every bit of the current value, using an 8-bit operand.<br>BUFFER leaves the value unchanged; NOT inverts all 8 bits.<br>AND, OR, NAND, NOR, XOR and XNOR combine the current value with the operand bit by bit.<br>Start from the given initial value, apply the gates in order, and print the final 8-bit value as a decimal integer.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> The number of gates <var>N</var>.<br><strong>Line 2:</strong> The initial 8-bit value <var>V</var> (0 to 255).<br><strong>Next N lines:</strong> A gate name and an 8-bit operand, space-separated.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> The final 8-bit value as a decimal integer.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &lt;= <var>N</var> &lt;= 12<br>0 &lt;= <var>V</var> &lt;= 255<br>0 &lt;= operand &lt;= 255</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">4\n32\nNAND 241\nNOT 194\nXNOR 107\nXNOR 48</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">123</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   